    "answer": {
      "short": "$3 \\times 10^8$; take the positive square root for the speed.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}c^2 &= \\frac{E}{m}\\\\c^2 &= \\frac{4.05 \\times 10^{18}}{45}\\\\c^2 &= 9 \\times 10^{16}\\\\c &= 3 \\times 10^8\\end{align*}$$\nTake the positive square root because $c$ represents a speed.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
